{"id": "a19", "question": "What is the postfix form of the sample input A+B*C in the stack experiment?", "answerable": true, "error": null, "status": "answered", "reason": "grounded", "answer": "According to [S1], the procedure for converting an infix expression to postfix is:\n\n1. Scan the infix expression from left to right.\n2. Operands go directly to the output.\n3. Push an opening parenthesis.\n4. On a closing parenthesis, pop operators to the output until the opening parenthesis.\n5. For an operator, pop operators of higher or equal precedence before pushing it.\n\nApplying this procedure to the sample input A+B*C:\n\n1. Scan from left to right: A, B, C\n2. Operands go directly to the output: A, B, C\n3. Push an opening parenthesis: (A, B, C)\n4. On a closing parenthesis, pop operators to the output until the opening parenthesis: (A, B, C) -> A, B, C\n5. For an operator, pop operators of higher or equal precedence before pushing it: Since there are no operators with higher or equal precedence, the output remains A, B, C.\n\nTherefore, the postfix form of the sample input A+B*C is ABC*.", "best_score": 0.7575, "support": 0.781, "retrieved": [{"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 3, "score": 0.7575}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.5833}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 2, "score": 0.5827}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 4, "score": 0.5599}, {"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 1, "score": 0.556}], "citations": [{"filename": "DEMO-Data-Structures-Lab-Manual.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "EXPERIMENT 3 - STACK AND INFIX TO POSTFIX CONVERSION"}], "attestation_index": 121, "isolated": false, "ttft_s": 27.204801100000623, "total_s": 65.078, "hit": true, "citation_correct": [true], "keyword_match": false}
